{"name":"Foam","hex":"#d0eae8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"foam","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A substance composed of a large collection of bubbles or their solidified remains, especially:","A collection of small bubbles created when the surface of a body of water is moved by tides, wind, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form or emit foam.","To spew saliva as foam; to foam at the mouth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foam"}],"entries":[{"title":"Foam","blocks":[{"text":"Foam is a two-phase material system and a type of dispersed media, consisting of gas cells dispersed in a continuous liquid or solid phase to form a cellular structure. In most foams, the gas occupies most of the volume and is divided into bubbles separated by thin films of liquid or solid material."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/The_top_of_foamy_drink_%28Unsplash%29.jpg/330px-The_top_of_foamy_drink_%28Unsplash%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foam","wikidata":"Q215414"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Order_and_Chaos.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Order_and_Chaos.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Order_and_Chaos.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Order_and_Chaos.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Order_and_Chaos.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Order_and_Chaos.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Order and disorder of bubbles in a surface foam","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOrder_and_Chaos.tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Marangoni_Effect_of_a_Film.png/330px-Marangoni_Effect_of_a_F